# ============================================================
#  Phase 2b vertical slice (design §13): the world loop in the new
#  format. The Evocation course (3 levels), the Duelling Circle, the
#  Library Assistant job, five campus places, break plans, the
#  Royal Library internship, the thesis, and a four-event arc
#  (The Bell Under the Water). Uses cast roles, say[npc],
#  present(place), queue within … and unqueue.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Evocation (track: evocation) ----------------

@event evo_first_spark
title: The First Spark
track: evocation
level: 1
lesson: lumenhold
class: routine
tone: light
art: flame
tags: class magic
scene: A lecture hall with scorch marks on every desk, students holding their palms up as if testing for rain.
text: Evocation I begins with a single instruction from the lectern: "Make heat. Not fire. Heat." Half the class makes nothing. One student makes a small, apologetic fire.
> left: Aim for heat, carefully
  arcana +small
  say: Your palm warms like a stone left in the sun. The lecturer nods, which is better than most get.
> right: Aim for fire, boldly
  challenge exam standard-1 wild:
    win:
      arcana +medium
      renown +tiny
      say: A neat little flame, exactly where you meant it. The lecturer writes your name down. Approvingly, you hope.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      arcana +tiny
      say: Your sleeve learns more about fire than you do. The lecture continues around the smell.

@event evo_puddle_drill
title: Puddle Drill
track: evocation
level: 1
lesson: mirror_lake
class: routine
tone: light
art: wave
tags: class magic
scene: Students crouched over puddles in a stone courtyard, trying to make the water stand up.
text: Tidecalling half of the course: a puddle each, and the task of making it stand up and stay up. Yours trembles, considers it, and lies back down.
> left: Practise until it stands
  grind arcana
  say: By the end of the hour your puddle stands like a sulky child. It counts.
> right: Watch the student next to you
  arcana +tiny
  guile +tiny
  say: You learn their trick, and also that they hum while they cast. You hum too. It works, inexplicably.

@event evo_misfire
title: Misfire
track: evocation
level: 1
class: incident
tone: tense
art: bolt
tags: class danger
scene: A lecture hall filling with steam after a spell meets a bucket of water at the wrong moment.
text: Someone's tidecalling meets someone else's flame in the middle of the room. The hall fills with scalding steam and twenty students who all have opinions.
> left: Shield the front row
  health -small
  alignment +tiny
  renown +small
  say: You take the worst of it on your sleeves. The front row looks at you the way people look at lifeboats.
> right: Get out and open the windows
  mood -tiny
  say: The steam pours out into the courtyard and becomes, briefly, a very small cloud with a grudge.

@event evo_tide_wall
title: The Tide Wall
track: evocation
level: 2
lesson: mirror_lake
class: routine
tone: tense
art: wave
tags: class magic
scene: A student holding back a wall of lake water on the shore while classmates watch from behind them.
text: Evocation II takes the class to the lakeshore. The exercise: raise a wall of water and hold it while a classmate walks past behind it. Your classmate looks nervous. So do you.
> left: Hold it steady
  challenge exam standard steady:
    win:
      arcana +medium
      say: The wall holds. Your classmate walks past dry and amazed. You let it down gently, which is the hard part.
    lose:
      health -small
      mood -small
      say: The wall holds until it doesn't, and comes down on both of you. Your classmate is very wet and very gracious about it. You shiver until dinner.
> right: Ask to go second
  arcana +small
  say: You watch three people do it first and learn from all of their mistakes.

@event evo_lattice
title: The Flame Lattice
track: evocation
level: 2
lesson: founders_seal
class: routine
tone: light
art: flame
tags: class study
scene: Interlocking threads of fire hanging in the air of a lecture hall like a glowing net.
text: Fire woven into a lattice, each strand holding the others up. The lecturer says the founders built wards like this. The lecturer also says you have twenty minutes.
> left: Build it slowly
  lore +small
  arcana +small
  mood -small
  say: Your lattice is small and ugly and holds perfectly. The lecturer says "Founder-ish," which you choose to take as praise.
> right: Build it big
  chance even:
    arcana +large
    say: {~It's magnificent for nine seconds.|It holds just long enough for everyone to see it.} Then the strands find each other and the whole thing sighs into sparks, and you understand exactly why.
  else:
    mood -small
    health -tiny
    say: The strands find each other in the first second, and the whole thing goes up in your face. You spend the rest of the lesson picking sparks out of your hair.

@event evo_storm_pairing
title: Storm Pairing
track: evocation
level: 3
class: milestone
tone: tense
art: bolt
tags: class duel
cast:
  partner: any where (tagged(partner, student) or tagged(partner, prefect))
scene: Two students on a windswept tower top, one calling rain, the other calling lightning, the sky between them churning.
text: Advanced Evocation pairs students for a storm: one calls the rain, the other the lightning, and neither is allowed to let go first. You're paired with {partner}.
> left: Call the lightning
  challenge exam standard+1 wild:
    win:
      arcana +large
      rel partner +small
      say: The storm answers both of you at once. {partner} laughs into the wind, soaked and astonished.
      say[lyra]: The storm answers both of you at once. Lyra looks at you as though you've finally said something worth hearing.
    lose:
      health -medium
      rel partner +tiny
      say: The lightning goes where it likes. You both spend an afternoon in the infirmary, comparing burns.
> right: Call the rain, and let them lead
  arcana +medium
  rel partner +small
  say: You hold the rain steady while {partner} draws the lightning down. Afterwards {they} thank{s} you for not trying to steal it.

@event evo_final_practical
title: The Final Practical
track: evocation
level: 3
when: month == 4 or month == 10
class: story
tone: tense
art: flame
tags: class exam
scene: An examination hall cleared of desks, a single student facing three examiners and a target dummy made of ice.
text: The last practical of Advanced Evocation: melt an ice dummy without touching the floor around it. Professor Thorne is on the panel, and he is not blinking.
> left: Fire, precisely
  challenge exam standard+1 steady:
    win:
      arcana +large
      study evocation +medium
      rel thorne +small
      say: The ice runs off the dummy and not a drop touches the floor. Thorne says "Hm," and writes something underlined.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: The dummy melts, and so does a fair part of the floor. Thorne writes something with a question mark.
> right: Water, patiently
  arcana +medium
  lore +small
  say: You draw the cold out of the ice with water instead of fire. It takes twice as long. The panel watches every minute.

# ---------------- Duelling Circle (track: duelling) ----------------

@event duel_first_practice
title: Footwork
track: duelling
rank: 1
when: around(lyra)
class: routine
tone: light
art: duel
tags: club duel
scene: A duelling hall with chalk circles on the floor and practice dummies with names painted on their chests.
text: Lyra runs practice like a general. "Footwork," she says. "If your feet are wrong, your spell is a rumour." She pairs you with a dummy called Gerald the Second.
> left: Drill footwork
  vigor +small
  perform track +small
  mood -tiny
  say: Two hours of stepping in circles. Gerald the Second wins every round. Your feet, however, are now correct.
> right: Spar for real
  challenge combat vs lyra.vigor -1:
    win:
      vigor +medium
      rel lyra +small
      say: You land a clean disarm on your partner. Across the hall, Lyra raises an eyebrow, which is her version of a standing ovation.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: You spend the evening relearning which way is up. Lyra says that's the first lesson anyway.

@event duel_footwork_feud
title: The Footwork Feud
track: duelling
when: around(lyra) and around(bram)
class: routine
tone: tense
art: duel
tags: club rival
scene: Two students arguing in the middle of a duelling circle while the rest of the club pretends not to listen.
text: Bram says the Circle's footwork is "Emberhall nonsense" and Lyra says Bram's footwork is "a hazard to shipping". Both of them look at you to settle it.
> left: Side with Lyra
  rel lyra +small
  rel bram -small
  npc_rel lyra bram -tiny
  say: Lyra nods as if this were obvious. Bram takes a demerit book out of his pocket, looks at it, and puts it back. Progress.
> right: Side with Bram
  rel bram +small
  rel lyra -small
  say: Bram looks startled to be agreed with. Lyra looks at you like a puzzle she will solve later, with fire.

@event duel_fixture
title: Fixture Against Thornwick
track: duelling
rank: 2
class: milestone
tone: tense
art: trophy
tags: club duel festival
scene: A duelling green with rival banners, students from both academies packed onto benches.
text: Thornwick Academy's duelling team has crossed the hills for a fixture. The Circle needs one more duellist in the line-up, and the captain is looking at you.
> left: Duel for the Circle
  challenge combat adept-:
    win:
      renown +medium
      perform track +medium
      say: You win your bout, and the Circle wins the fixture by a whisker. Someone carries you a few steps before remembering they don't like you.
    partial:
      renown +small
      perform track +small
      say: A draw. The Circle loses by one bout, but nobody blames you, and {around(lyra): Lyra|the captain} says "acceptable" twice.
    lose:
      health -small
      mood -small
      say: The Thornwick duellist is very good and very polite about it, and every bruise you collect is a polite one. You hate both.
> right: Offer to be the reserve
  perform track +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: You hold coats and bring water. It turns out reserves see everything, including how Thornwick cheats.
> up[wildfire]: Let the fire run
  renown +medium
  perform track +small
  health -tiny
  say: You hold the fire until it bites, and then let it go. It runs across the hall and through the Thornwick duellist's wards like paper. The Circle goes mad. Your sleeve is on fire, which you notice afterwards.

@event duel_captain_call
title: The Captain's Question
track: duelling
rank: 2
class: milestone
tone: warm
art: duel
tags: club
scene: An empty duelling hall at night, two students sitting on the edge of a chalk circle.
text: After practice, the captain sits beside you. "When I graduate, someone has to run this place," she says. "Someone who turns up. You turn up."
> left: Say you'll think about it
  perform track +small
  rank_xp track +medium
  say: "Think fast," she says. "Feet first, then spells." You're fairly sure that's a yes.
> right: Say you're not the type
  mood +tiny
  say: "Nobody's the type," she says. "That's why it has to be someone who turns up."

# ---------------- Library Assistant (track: library_assistant) ----------------

@event lib_shelving_rush
title: The Shelving Rush
track: library_assistant
when: month == 4 or month == 10
class: routine
tone: light
art: book
tags: job study
scene: A library cart overflowing with returned books, a student pushing it at a run between towering shelves.
text: Exam week, and every book in the library has been borrowed, read and returned at once. The cart is taller than you are. Footnote is sitting on top of it.
> left: Shelve properly
  wage
  lore +small
  perform track +small
  mood -small
  say: Every book in its place by closing. Footnote has moved to the top shelf to supervise.
> right: Shelve quickly
  wage
  perform track -tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: The books are on shelves. Most of them are even on the right shelves. Someone will find out in a decade.
> up[animate]: Animate the cart
  wage
  perform track +small
  mood -tiny
  say: The cart trundles off by itself, putting books back in roughly the right places, and you follow behind it fixing the rough parts. It takes everything you've got to keep it from shelving Footnote.

@event lib_overdue_mage
title: The Overdue Mage
track: library_assistant
class: routine
tone: light
art: hourglass
tags: job
scene: An elderly mage at the library desk clutching a book that is sixty years overdue.
text: An old mage returns a book sixty years overdue and asks, with great dignity, what the fine is. The ledger says the fine is more than the library.
> left: Waive it
  wage
  perform track -tiny
  mood +small
  say: The old mage thanks you and leaves a sweet on the desk. Later you find out he taught Professor Thorne.
> right: Charge it, by the book
  wage
  gold +small
  perform track +small
  say: The mage pays in coins so old the bank has to look them up. The head librarian is delighted, and gives you the collector's share of the fine, as is tradition.

@event lib_footnote_strike
title: Footnote Goes on Strike
track: library_assistant
class: incident
tone: light
art: cat
tags: job
scene: A large library cat lying across a reference desk, refusing to move, while students queue in front of it.
text: Footnote has lain down across the reference desk and will not move. Students are queueing. The cat has made its demands clear: none.
> left: Bribe him with fish
  wage
  gold -tiny
  perform track +small
  say: Footnote accepts the fish, the apology and the chair you bring him. The queue resumes.
> right: Work around him
  wage
  perform track -tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: You stamp books on the far end of the desk for an hour. Footnote watches with the calm of a cat who has won.

# ---------------- Places ----------------

@event court_fountain_freeze
title: The Frozen Fountain
place: courtyard
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: snow
tags: mystery
scene: A courtyard fountain frozen mid-splash, the water hanging in the air like glass.
text: The courtyard fountain has frozen in the middle of a splash. The water hangs in the air like glass. A first-year is trying to lick it.
> left: Stop the first-year
  health -tiny
  alignment +small
  say: You pull the first-year away just as the ice cracks. For a moment you'd swear you saw a black star reflected in it.
> right: Study the ice
  lore +small
  say: The ice is colder than ice should be. Your notes say "colder than ice should be" three times.
> up[hoarfrost]: Freeze the first-year free
  alignment +tiny
  arcana +small
  say: You put a hand on the ice and pull the cold back into yourself, just round the first-year's tongue. They come free with a pop and a look of betrayal at the fountain. Your hand aches with cold all afternoon.

@event court_rumour_mill
title: The Rumour Mill
place: courtyard
class: routine
tone: light
art: group
tags: social
cast:
  gossip: present(place) where tagged(gossip, peer)
scene: Students huddled around the courtyard fountain trading whispers, one of them clearly enjoying it most.
text: {gossip} has news, which is to say gossip, which is to say three different stories about the same broken window. "You'll want to hear this," {they} say{s}.
> left: Listen to all of it
  rel gossip +small
  mood +small
  say: You hear all three stories. Two are true. One is about you.
  say[nessa]: You hear all three stories. Nessa is already writing the fourth.
> right: Make up a better one
  guile +small
  rel gossip +tiny
  renown +tiny
  alignment -tiny
  say: Your story is better than all three. By dinner it's the official version.
> up[candour]: Ask what really happened
  rel gossip -tiny
  lore +small
  say: You ask the right question and {gossip} tells you the truth, startled: the window broke because someone sneezed during a levitation. It is the least interesting story of the four. {They} look{s} at you as if you'd cheated.

@event lake_skimming
title: Skimming Stones
place: lakeshore
class: routine
tone: warm
art: wave
tags: nature
cast:
  friend: any where tagged(friend, peer) and rel(friend) >= 6
scene: Two students skimming stones across a perfectly still lake at dusk.
text: {friend} is skimming stones on the Mirror Lake. The water is so still each stone leaves rings that go on forever. "Seven," {they} say{s}. "Beat that."
> left: Try to beat it
  challenge duel apprentice wild:
    win:
      rel friend +small
      mood +small
      say: Nine skips. {friend} demands a rematch and gets one. The afternoon disappears into stones.
    lose:
      rel friend +small
      mood +tiny
      say: Your stone sinks with great dignity. {friend} laughs until {they} have to sit down.
> right: Just watch the rings
  mood +small
  rel friend +tiny
  say: You sit and watch the rings spread until the light goes. Neither of you says much. It's one of the good afternoons.

@event lake_reflection_bet
title: The Reflection Bet
place: lakeshore
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: mirror
tags: mystery
scene: A student staring into a still lake where their reflection appears to be holding a coin.
text: Your reflection in the Mirror Lake is holding a coin you don't have. It flips it. It catches it. It offers it to you.
> left: Take the coin
  gold +small
  alignment -tiny
  say: The coin is real, and cold, and you can't remember putting it in your pocket.
> right: Shake your head
  alignment +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: Your reflection shrugs, pockets the coin and walks out of the frame before you do.
> up[sleight]: Lift it before it offers
  gold +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You lift the coin from your reflection's hand before it can offer it. The reflection looks at its empty hand, then at you, deeply affronted. For a week you can't quite meet your own eye in the washroom mirror.

@event ref_food_fight
title: Pudding Diplomacy
place: refectory
class: routine
tone: light
art: meal
tags: social
scene: A refectory mid-food-fight, puddings in the air, a prefect rising slowly from behind a table.
text: A pudding sails across the refectory and lands in Bram's lap. The hall goes silent. Every eye turns to the table it came from, which is yours.
> left: Own up
  alignment +tiny
  rel bram +small
  renown +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: Bram writes you a demerit, then pauses. "Good throw," he says, almost without wanting to.
> right: Throw another
  renown +small
  rel bram -small
  mood +small
  say: The second pudding starts a war that the refectory will talk about for years. Historians will argue about who won. You know.
> up[rapport]: Turn the hall with a joke
  renown +small
  rel bram +tiny
  say: You stand up, bow to Bram, and say the pudding was meant as a tribute. The hall laughs, and so, against his will, does Bram. He fishes the cherry out of his lap and eats it.

@event ref_cook_secret
title: The Cook's Secret
place: refectory
class: routine
tone: warm
art: cup
tags: home
scene: A huge kitchen behind the refectory, an enormous cook stirring a pot with a spoon the size of an oar.
text: The cook catches you lingering by the kitchen door. "You look like someone who misses proper soup," she says, and hands you a bowl before you can deny it.
> left: Eat it slowly
  health +small
  mood +small
  say: It tastes like the kitchen at home. You don't say so. She can tell anyway.
> right: Ask for the recipe
  alchemy +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: "Ha," says the cook, which means no, which means you'll have to keep coming back.
> up[candour]: Ask for the honest recipe
  alchemy +small
  mood +tiny
  say: The cook tells you the truth before she can stop herself: the secret is a spoon of the faculty's good sherry. She laughs, then makes you promise. You promise, and get a second bowl.

@event obs_comet_watch
slot: evening
title: The Comet Watch
place: observatory
class: routine
tone: warm
art: planet
tags: magic
scene: The brass dome of an observatory open to the night, a student at the eyepiece, another beside them with a notebook.
text: A comet is due tonight and the observatory is full of students pretending they came for the science. The telescope has a queue. The roof has a view.
> left: Queue for the telescope
  lore +small
  mood -tiny
  say: Your turn at the eyepiece lasts thirty seconds. The comet's tail is green. You'll remember it longer than most lectures.
> right: Watch from the roof
  mood +small
  rel kael +tiny
  say: The comet crosses the sky slowly, like it's looking for something. Kael is already on the roof. He moves over to make room.
> up[foresight]: Foresee where it will cross
  lore +small
  mood +small
  say: You look a moment ahead and point at an empty patch of sky. Everyone on the roof looks, and the comet crosses exactly there. Half the roof claps. The other half accuses you of reading the charts.

@event obs_star_chart
title: The Missing Star
place: observatory
class: story
tone: eerie
art: star
tags: mystery magic
scene: An old star chart spread on a desk, one constellation with a careful empty circle drawn where a star should be.
text: An old star chart in the observatory archive has a circle drawn where a star should be, with a note in faded ink: "It eats the light. Do not chart it."
> left: Copy the chart
  lore +small
  say: You copy it carefully. That night you dream of a circle with nothing inside it, waiting.
> right: Put it back
  mood +tiny
  say: You return it to the drawer. The drawer feels colder when you close it.

@event green_mandrake_choir
title: The Mandrake Choir
place: greenhouses
when: around(tobias)
class: routine
tone: light
art: leaf
tags: nature
scene: A greenhouse bench of potted mandrakes wearing tiny earmuffs, a student conducting them with a pencil.
text: Tobias has taught the greenhouse mandrakes to scream in harmony. He would like your opinion. The mandrakes would like an audience.
> left: Conduct a verse
  rel tobias +small
  health -tiny
  say: You conduct one verse. Your ears ring for a day. Tobias says it's the best performance they've given.
> right: Wear earmuffs and listen
  rel tobias +tiny
  mood +small
  say: Through the earmuffs it sounds almost beautiful. Tobias is so proud he cries a little.

@event green_moonflower_sprout
title: A Moonflower Seedling
place: greenhouses
class: routine
tone: warm
art: flower
tags: nature
scene: A tiny silver-leaved seedling in a clay pot, glowing faintly in a dark greenhouse.
text: In a forgotten corner of the greenhouse, a moonflower seed has sprouted on its own, eleven years early. It glows faintly when you lean over it.
> left: Pot it and look after it
  alchemy +small
  mood +small
  say: You give it a pot, a label and a name. It glows a little brighter when you visit.
> right: Tell Tobias
  when: around(tobias)
  rel tobias +medium
  say: Tobias is speechless, then very loud. The seedling gets a sign, a fence and a rota.
> up[bramble]: Entangle a hedge round it
  alchemy +small
  say: A ring of thorns comes up round the seedling, knee-high and very sure of itself. Nobody is treading on this one by accident. The seedling glows a little brighter, or you imagine it does.

# ---------------- Break days ----------------

@event castle_empty_halls
title: Empty Halls
plan: castle
class: routine
tone: warm
art: tower
tags: home
scene: A long castle corridor in the holidays, dust in sunbeams, one student walking alone.
text: The castle in the holidays is enormous and quiet. Your footsteps echo down corridors you've never been alone in. A door you've never noticed is standing open.
> left: Go through the door
  guile +small
  mood +tiny
  discover seventh_tower
  say: It leads to a stair that leads to a locked door that leads, you're almost sure, to the seventh tower.
> right: Read in the window seat
  lore +small
  mood +small
  say: You read all day in a window seat with the whole lake below you. The best kind of nothing.

@event castle_skeleton_crew
title: The Skeleton Crew
plan: castle
class: routine
tone: light
art: meal
tags: home
scene: A handful of staff and students sharing a long table in a nearly empty great hall.
text: Supper in the holidays is one table in the Great Hall: you, three other students, the cook, two prefects and Old Maud, who has brought her goat.
> left: Sit next to Maud
  rel maud +small
  mood +small
  say: Maud tells a story about the frozen spring that she's never told the term-time students. Bartholomew eats your napkin.
> right: Play cards with the prefects
  gold +small
  guile +tiny
  say: The prefects play cards like they enforce rules: badly and with great confidence. You win dessert and most of their pocket money.

@event home_family_supper
title: Supper at Home
place: home_cottage
class: routine
tone: warm
art: meal
tags: home
scene: A crowded kitchen table, a family passing dishes, a student back from the academy being asked too many questions.
text: Supper at home. Everyone wants to know what you've learned. You try to explain evocation to an aunt who thinks it's a kind of cheese.
> left: Show them a spell
  mood +small
  arcana +tiny
  say: You light every candle in the room at once. Your aunt applauds and asks if you can do it with cheese.
> right: Just listen
  mood +medium
  health +tiny
  say: You let them talk. You'd forgotten how loud and how good it is.

@event home_old_friend
title: An Old Friend
place: home_fields
class: routine
tone: warm
art: leaf
tags: home
scene: Two old friends sitting on a field wall at sunset, one in academy robes, the other in work clothes.
text: Your oldest friend is sitting on the wall at the edge of the fields, exactly where you left them. "So," they say. "Are you a wizard now, or what?"
> left: Tell them everything
  mood +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: You talk until the stars come out. They want to hear about the lake most of all.
> right: Ask about their life instead
  mood +small
  charm +small
  say: They've been busy too: a farm, a fiancé, a goat that bites. Your life isn't the only one that grew.

@event home_market_day
title: Market Day
place: home_market
class: routine
tone: light
art: coin
tags: home money
scene: A small country market, a student in academy robes being stared at by stallholders.
text: Market day in town. A stallholder recognises your academy robes and asks if you can do anything about his leaky roof. For a price.
> left: Fix it with magic
  gold +small
  arcana +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: The roof is dry, the stallholder is thrilled and you are slightly scorched. He pays in apples and coins.
> right: Just buy sweets
  gold -tiny
  mood +small
  say: The sweet shop still sells your favourites. You eat them on the bridge like you used to.

@event work_double_shift
title: The Double Shift
plan: work
class: routine
tone: tense
art: coin
tags: job money
scene: A student asleep on their feet behind a counter, a clock on the wall showing a very late hour.
text: Holiday shifts pay double and feel triple. It's your second shift today and the evening rush hasn't started.
> left: Push through
  gold +medium
  health -small
  mood -small
  say: You push through. The coins are heavy in your pocket and your feet are heavy everywhere else.
> right: Swap the shift
  mood +small
  say: A colleague takes it for a favour you'll owe later. You sleep for eleven hours.

# ---------------- The Royal Library internship (plan: internship) ----------------

@event intern_first_assignment
title: The First Assignment
track: intern_royal_library
class: routine
tone: light
art: book
tags: study
scene: A vast underground archive, a supervisor handing a student a list longer than their arm.
text: Your supervisor at the Royal Library hands you a list of forty uncatalogued boxes. "Find out what's in them," she says. "Carefully. One of them is probably alive."
> left: Work through the boxes
  wage
  lore +medium
  mood -small
  say: Box thirty-one is alive. It's a very small, very old dictionary that bites. You catalogue it.
> right: Ask the other interns
  wage
  charm +small
  lore +small
  mood -tiny
  say: The other interns have a system, a rota and a song. You learn all three.

@event intern_index_maze
title: The Index Maze
track: intern_royal_library
class: milestone
tone: tense
art: map
tags: study mystery
scene: A student lost between endless shelves underground, following an index card trail by lamplight.
text: A cross-reference in the archive leads to another, and another, and another, deeper under the city. The last card is about the founders of Lumenhold.
> left: Follow it to the end
  wage
  challenge research adept:
    win:
      lore +large
      say: At the end is a letter from a founder about "the seventh lock". You copy it with shaking hands.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: The trail ends at a missing card. Somebody took it. Recently.
> right: Report it to your supervisor
  wage
  lore +small
  perform track +small
  say: Your supervisor reads the card, goes pale, thanks you for your care, and writes a letter to the headmistress of Lumenhold.

# ---------------- Thesis (track: thesis) ----------------

@event thesis_proposal
title: The Proposal
track: thesis
when: progress(thesis) < 30
class: routine
tone: tense
art: scroll
tags: study
scene: A desk covered in drafts, one page with a single sentence circled many times.
text: Your thesis proposal is due. Professor Thorne wants one sentence that says what you'll find out. You have eleven sentences and none of them is it.
> left: Rewrite it all night
  progress track +medium
  health -small
  say: At dawn you have one sentence. Thorne reads it twice. "Yes," he says. "That."
> right: Hand in what you have
  progress track +small
  rel thorne -tiny
  say: Thorne reads all eleven sentences and circles the fourth. "That one," he says. "Next time, only that one."

@event thesis_lab_night
title: Late in the Lab
track: thesis
class: routine
tone: tense
art: candle
tags: study
scene: A thesis laboratory at midnight, one carrel lit, a student surrounded by open books.
text: The thesis lab, long after everyone else has gone home: and your argument has a hole in it the size of the seventh tower.
> left: Find the hole
  progress track +medium
  mood -small
  say: You find it, fill it and find two more. That's progress, apparently.
> right: Go to bed
  rest
  progress track -small
  say: You sleep. In the morning the hole is still there, but you can see the edges of it.

# ---------------- The Bell Under the Water (arc: the_bell) ----------------

@event bell_first_ring
title: A Bell Under the Water
arc: the_bell
beat: 1
slot: night
class: story
tone: eerie
art: bell
tags: mystery
scene: A dark lakeshore at night, ripples spreading from the middle of the lake though nothing has fallen in.
text: In the middle of the night you hear a bell, low and slow, from the middle of the lake. Nobody else in your dormitory wakes up.
> left: Go down to the shore
  find bell_heard
  health -tiny
  say: The water is perfectly still. Then, once, a ring spreads out from the centre, as if the lake had been struck from below.
> right: Pull the blanket over your head
  find bell_heard
  mood -tiny
  say: It rings seven times. You count every one. In the morning you are the only one who remembers.

@event bell_maud_rope
title: Maud's Rope
arc: the_bell
beat: 2
slot: night
class: story
tone: eerie
art: bell
tags: mystery
cast:
  keeper: maud
scene: An old woman in a garden shed holding up a frayed, waterlogged bell-rope.
text: {keeper} shows you a rope, frayed and black with lake water, that she's kept in her shed for sixty years. "From the bell," she says. "It came up the night the lake froze. Someone cut it."
> left: Ask who cut it
  find bell_rope
  rel keeper +small
  flag bell_asked
  find lead_maud_answer
  say: "That," says {keeper}, "is the question I've been asking for sixty years." She promises to tell you what she knows, when she's ready. "Come by the cottage, dearie. Not tonight."
> right: Leave her to her memories
  find bell_rope
  rel keeper +tiny
  say: You leave her with the rope in her lap. She doesn't notice you go.

@event bell_answer
title: What Maud Remembers
# Feedback 2026-10-16: no longer on a timer. Asking about the rope leaves a lead; she tells you at her cottage.
place: maud_cottage
when: flag(bell_asked) and met(maud)
weight: 18
actor: maud
class: story
tone: warm
art: lantern
tags: mystery
scene: An old woman and a student sitting by a cottage fire, a waterlogged rope coiled between them.
text: {npc} has the kettle on before you knock. "The rope," she says, once the tea is poured. "Edmund cut it. To stop the bell ringing the thing awake. It went on ringing anyway."
> ok: Listen
  rel npc +small
  mood -tiny
  say: She talks until the light goes. When she's finished, she seems lighter, and you seem to be carrying something.

@event bell_drowned
title: The Diving Bell
arc: the_bell
beat: 3
slot: night
class: story
tone: tense
art: wave
tags: mystery danger
scene: A student in a borrowed diving helmet standing at the end of a jetty over black water.
text: The bell has rung every night for a week. The boathouse has an old diving helmet and a rope. The lake is very dark and very still.
> left: Dive
  challenge research adept- wild:
    win:
      find bell_name
      lore +medium
      say: Far down, the bell lies on its side, and around its rim, letters: a name you don't know. You surface gasping, and you keep the name.
    lose:
      health -medium
      find lead_bell_dive
      say: The cold drives you back up before you see anything. Old Maud is waiting on the jetty with a blanket and a look. The helmet stays in the boathouse, if you want to try again.
> right: Wait for the bell to stop
  mood -small
  lore +small
  find lead_bell_dive
  say: You wait for a week, listening from the shore, until you know its rhythm by heart. It doesn't stop. Something in you decides it will have to be you, next time: the helmet is still in the boathouse.

@event bell_silence
title: The Bell Calls
arc: the_bell
beat: 4
slot: night
when: clue(bell_name) or clue(bell_rope)
class: story
tone: eerie
art: bell
tags: mystery
# Feedback 2026-10-16: beat 4 no longer ends the arc by itself. It names where to go; the silencing is played at the
# lakeshore after hours (bell_laid_to_rest), with the name or the rope.
scene: A dormitory window at night, the Mirror Lake beyond it silver under the moon, rings spreading across the water.
text: The bell is ringing every night now, louder, and tonight it rings your way: you can feel it in your teeth. {clue(bell_name): You have the name from its rim.|You have Maud's rope.} You know, the way you know your own handwriting, that it wants you at the lakeshore after dark.
> ok: Tonight, then
  find lead_bell_shore
  say: You lie awake counting the rings. Seven, always seven. Whenever you go down to the shore after dark, it will be waiting.

@event bell_laid_to_rest
title: The Bell Falls Silent
arc: the_bell
place: lakeshore
time: evening midnight
when: seen(bell_silence) > 0 and (clue(bell_name) or clue(bell_rope)) and not flag(bell_silenced)
repeat: 1
weight: 20
type: menu
class: story
tone: warm
art: bell
tags: mystery
scene: The Mirror Lake at dusk, perfectly still, a student standing at the water's edge with a lantern.
text: The shore is empty and the lake is glass. Then the bell begins, slow and low, from the very middle. {clue(bell_name) and clue(bell_rope): You have the name from its rim and Maud's rope in your hands.|{clue(bell_name): You have the name from its rim.|You have Maud's rope, cut sixty years ago.}}
> name: Say the name over the water
  when: clue(bell_name)
  flag bell_silenced
  mood +medium
  alignment +small
  rel maud +small
  say: You say the name from the bell's rim out loud. The bell rings once more, as if answering to it, and then the lake is just a lake. Somewhere in her cottage, you think, Maud sleeps through the night.
> rope: Give the rope back to the lake
  when: clue(bell_rope)
  flag bell_silenced
  mood +small
  alignment +small
  health -tiny
  say: You wade in to your knees and let the rope sink. It goes down straight, as if something below were pulling it home. The bell rings one last time, muffled, and stops. The cold stays in your legs all night.
> wait: Not tonight
  say: You stand at the shore until the ringing stops on its own, and go back up the lawn. It will ring again tomorrow.

@event bell_dive_again
title: The Helmet in the Boathouse
arc: the_bell
place: boathouse
time: afternoon evening
when: clue(lead_bell_dive) and not clue(bell_name)
repeat: 2
weight: 16
class: story
tone: tense
art: wave
tags: mystery danger
scene: An old brass diving helmet on a boathouse workbench beside a coil of rope, the lake glinting through the open doors.
text: The old diving helmet is where you left it, on the workbench by the doors. Somebody has oiled the rope since last time. The lake is still, and under it the bell is waiting.
> left: Dive again
  hint: You know the cold now.
  challenge research adept- wild +1 if clue(lead_bell_dive):
    win:
      find bell_name
      lore +medium
      say: You go down slower this time, and further. The bell lies on its side, and around its rim, letters: a name you don't know. You surface gasping, and you keep the name.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: The cold finds you again, halfway down. You come up blue and shaking, with nothing but the certainty that it's down there.
> right: Not today
  say: You put the helmet back on the bench. The bell can wait one more day. It has waited sixty years.

@event bell_echo_lakeshore
title: Rings on Still Water
place: lakeshore
when: clue(bell_heard) and not flag(bell_silenced)
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: wave
tags: mystery
scene: A calm lake at dusk, perfect rings spreading from its centre although nothing has fallen in, a student crouched at the water's edge.
text: The lake is flat calm, and still rings spread from its middle, slow and even, like the ripples from a bell that nobody hears. A heron on the shallows lifts its head at each one.
> left: Count the rings
  lore +small
  mood -tiny
  say: Seven, then a pause, then seven. The heron counts them too, you'd swear. You walk back up the lawn with the number stuck in your head.
> right: Skim a stone across them
  mood +small
  say: Your stone skips four times and sinks in the middle of a ring. For a moment the rings stop. Then they start again, patient as anything.

@event bell_echo_boathouse
title: The Boats Keep Time
place: boathouse
when: clue(bell_heard) and not flag(bell_silenced)
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: wave
tags: mystery
scene: Rowing boats tied in an old boathouse, all knocking gently against their posts in the same rhythm, a student listening in the doorway.
text: Inside the boathouse every boat is knocking against its post in the same slow rhythm, though there's no wind and the water outside is still. Knock, knock, knock: seven, then a pause.
> left: Steady the boats
  vigor +small
  health -tiny
  say: You go from boat to boat with wet sleeves, holding each one still. As soon as you let go, they take up the rhythm again.
> right: Sit and listen
  lore +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You sit on an upturned hull and listen until you can hear the bell under the knocking. It is very far down, and very patient.

@event bell_echo_cottage
title: Maud's Teacups
place: maud_cottage
when: clue(bell_heard) and met(maud) and not flag(bell_silenced)
class: routine
tone: warm
art: cup
tags: mystery
scene: A cottage dresser full of mismatched teacups, all trembling and chiming together, an old woman pretending not to notice.
text: In Maud's cottage the teacups on the dresser are chiming against each other, all together, though nobody has touched them. Maud pours your tea as if she can't hear a thing. "Biscuit, dearie?"
> left: Ask her about the cups
  rel maud +small
  mood -tiny
  say: "Old cups," says Maud. "Old lake." She looks at the window a long time. "They've done that since I was a girl, on the nights it rings. You get used to it. You don't."
> right: Help her wrap them in cloth
  rel maud +tiny
  mood +small
  say: You wrap every cup in an old tea towel. The chiming stops, and Maud's shoulders come down an inch. "There," she says. "Now we can hear ourselves think."
